# THE SIFREI ROWS on Deuteronomy 1:18-1:30 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 1 — THE OPENING SPEECH, 2026-09-15): piskaot 18-25 by POSITION — on
# 1:18-19 (18), 1:20-21 (19), 1:22 (20), 1:23 (21), 1:24 (22), 1:25-26 (23), 1:27 (24), 1:28-30 (25); twenty-four rows, each read in both
# files; the middah named. The shelf's Hebrew cut by consonants (deu_ink.SP_). The shelf's last row on chapter 1 is 25:8 on 1:30; NO piska
# on 1:31-3:22 — the next is 26 on 3:23.
from deu_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(18, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND I CHARGED YOU AT THAT TIME ALL THE THINGS YOU SHOULD DO" — THESE ARE THE TEN DISTINCTIONS BETWEEN MONEY CASES AND CAPITAL CASES. ({SP_(18, 1, "אלו", "עשרה", "דברים", "שבין", "דיני", "ממונות", "לדיני")} "these are the ten things between money cases and capital") — SANHEDRIN 4:1\'s list seated on 1:18 (the testing shelf named by the Sifrei: the Mishnah\'s table the answer sheet the compile keeps); the middah: the number read from \'all the things\' (the aggadic count).')
srow(18, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND WE JOURNEYED FROM HOREB THROUGH ALL THAT GREAT AND TERRIBLE WILDERNESS" — MEN WHO SAW SERPENTS LIKE BEAMS AND SCORPIONS LIKE BOWS, ROTTING AND THROWN BEFORE THEM — OF THEM HE SAYS "THAT GREAT AND TERRIBLE WILDERNESS"? IS IT NOT A FORTIORI: IF THINGS THAT DO NOT... I SUBDUED BEFORE THEM, THINGS THAT... HOW MUCH MORE! ({SP_(18, 2, "נחשים", "כקורות", "ועקרבים", "כקשתות")} "serpents like beams and scorpions like bows") — 8:15\'s serpents and scorpions read into 1:19\'s wilderness; the a-fortiori (I1) from the monstrous to the ordinary; the English reads the verse as encouragement.')
srow(19, 1, 'CONTEXT', '"AND I SAID TO YOU" (1:20) — NOT FROM MYSELF BUT FROM THE MOUTH OF THE HOLY ONE. The refrain.')
srow(19, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU HAVE COME TO THE HILL COUNTRY OF THE AMORITES WHICH THE LORD OUR GOD GIVES US" — A PARABLE: THE KING GAVE HIS SON TO A TUTOR WHO WALKED HIM ROUND: ALL THESE VINES ARE YOURS, ALL THESE OLIVES; TIRED OF SHOWING, HE SAID: ALL YOU SEE IS YOURS. SO FORTY YEARS MOSES SAID "THE LORD BRINGS YOU TO A GOOD LAND" (8:7); COME TO THE LAND HE SAID: YOU HAVE COME — IF YOU SAY THE TIME HAS NOT COME, IT HAS COME. ({SP_(19, 2, "משל", "למלך", "שמסר", "את", "בנו", "לפידגוג")} "a parable of a king who gave his son to a tutor") — \'you have come\' read as the promise arrived; the compile\'s clock: the forty years ended at 1:20.')
srow(19, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"SEE, THE LORD YOUR GOD HAS SET THE LAND BEFORE YOU" — NOT BY ESTIMATE NOR HEARSAY BUT WHAT YOU SEE WITH YOUR EYES. "GO UP, POSSESS" — AT ONCE! "GO UP, POSSESS AS THE LORD GOD OF YOUR FATHERS SPOKE TO YOU" (1:21). ({SP_(19, 3, "עלה", "רש", "מיד")} "go up, possess — at once") — the witness\'s charge (7:1) and the \'at once\' (2:2) at 1:21.')
srow(20, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU CAME NEAR TO ME, ALL OF YOU, AND SAID" — IN CONFUSION. ELSEWHERE "ALL THE HEADS OF YOUR TRIBES AND YOUR ELDERS CAME NEAR TO ME" (5:20) — THE YOUNG HONORING THE ELDERS, THE ELDERS THE HEADS; HERE "ALL OF YOU" — THE YOUNG SHOVING THE ELDERS, THE ELDERS THE HEADS. ({SP_(20, 1, "ילדים", "דוחפים", "את", "הזקנים")} "the young shoving the elders") — 1:22\'s \'all of you\' against 5:20\'s order: the same verb at two seats read by their difference (E7, the narrative verbal analogy); the ink: \'you came near to me, all of you\' one seat.')
srow(20, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"LET US SEND MEN BEFORE US TO SEARCH OUT THE LAND" — R. SHIMON: WRETCHED MEN, WHO SO ASKED FOR SPIES! WHEN YOU WERE IN A LAND OF DESERT AND PITS (Jeremiah 2:6) YOU ASKED NO SPIES; NOW ENTERING A GOOD AND BROAD LAND FLOWING WITH MILK AND HONEY, YOU ASK SPIES? ({SP_(20, 2, "עלובים", "בני", "אדם", "שכך", "בקשו", "להם", "מרגלים")} "wretched men, who so asked for themselves spies") — R. Shimon\'s scorn (23:1 the same); the spy-word the Sifrei\'s (the verse says \'search out\').')
srow(20, 3, 'CONTEXT', '"AND BRING US BACK WORD" — IN WHAT LANGUAGE THEY SPEAK. The word as the language.')
srow(20, 4, 'CONTEXT', '"THE WAY WE SHOULD GO UP" — NO WAY WITHOUT CROOKS, NO WAY WITHOUT AMBUSHES, NO WAY WITHOUT CROSSROADS. The road\'s three.')
srow(20, 5, 'CONTEXT', '"AND THE CITIES WE SHOULD COME TO" — TO KNOW BY WHICH WAY WE COME UPON THEM. The cities\' approach.')
srow(21, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE THING WAS GOOD IN MY EYES" — IN MY EYES, NOT IN THE OMNIPRESENT\'S. IF GOOD IN HIS EYES, WHY WRITTEN AMONG THE WORDS OF REBUKE? A PARABLE: SELL ME YOUR DONKEY — YES; ON TRIAL? — YES, COME, I WILL SHOW YOU HOW MUCH IT CARRIES ON THE HILL AND IN THE VALLEY; SEEING HIM HOLD NOTHING BACK, HE SAID: WOE, HE HOLDS NOTHING BACK ONLY TO CARRY OFF MY MONEY. ({SP_(21, 1, "בעיני", "היה", "טוב", "ולא", "בעיני", "מקום")} "in my eyes it was good and not in the eyes of the Omnipresent") — \'my eyes\' read as the limit of the approval; the parable\'s suspicion the people\'s.')
srow(21, 2, 'CONTEXT', '"AND I TOOK TWELVE MEN OF YOU" — OF THE CHOICEST, THE FINEST AMONG YOU. The twelve\'s quality.')
srow(21, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"ONE MAN PER TRIBE" — WHY? "TWELVE MEN" IS SAID! IT TELLS THAT THE TRIBE OF LEVI WAS NOT WITH THEM. ({SP_(21, 3, "מגיד", "שלא", "היה", "שבט", "לוי", "עמהם")} "it tells that the tribe of Levi was not with them") — the redundancy resolved (I5): twelve by tribe without Levi; the parser [12, 1] and Numbers 13\'s list (Levi absent) agree — the compile\'s census.')
srow(22, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THEY TURNED AND WENT UP TO THE HILL COUNTRY" — THE SPIES\' WAY IS TO GO UP THE HILL; SO RAHAB TO JOSHUA\'S MESSENGERS: "GO TO THE HILL LEST THE PURSUERS MEET YOU" (Joshua 2:16) — THE HOLY SPIRIT RESTED ON HER, ELSE HOW DID SHE KNOW THEY WOULD RETURN AFTER THREE DAYS? ({SP_(22, 1, "מגיד", "שדרך", "מרגלים", "לעלות", "בהר")} "it tells that the way of spies is to go up the hill") — Joshua 2\'s spies brought to 1:24 (the ink: the spy-verb\'s seats include Joshua 2:1).')
srow(22, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND CAME TO THE VALLEY OF ESHCOL" — NAMED FOR ITS END; SO "HE CAME TO THE MOUNTAIN OF GOD, HOREB" (Exodus 3:1) — NAMED FOR ITS END. ({SP_(22, 2, "מלמד", "שנקרא", "על", "שם", "סופו")} "it teaches that it was named after its end") — the anachronism of names resolved: Eshcol before the cluster, Horeb before the giving; the compile\'s naming rule.')
srow(22, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THEY SPIED IT OUT" — THEY WALKED IT IN FOUR ROWS, WARP AND WOOF. ({SP_(22, 3, "שהלכו", "בה", "ארבעה", "אומנים", "שתי", "וערב")} "that they walked it in four rows, warp and woof") — the spy-verb (piel, the ink) read as a method: the land gridded.')
srow(23, 1, 'CONTEXT', '"AND THEY TOOK OF THE FRUIT OF THE LAND IN THEIR HAND" — R. SHIMON: WRETCHED MEN, WHO SO TOOK IN THEIR HAND, AS ONE TAKES FIGS FOR AN ISSAR, GRAPES FOR AN ISSAR. R. Shimon\'s scorn (20:2 the same).')
srow(23, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND BROUGHT IT DOWN TO US" — THE LAND OF CANAAN IS HIGHER THAN ALL LANDS: "WE WILL SURELY GO UP" (Numbers 13:30), "THEY WENT UP AND TOURED" (13:21), "THEY WENT UP BY THE NEGEB" (13:22), "THEY WENT UP FROM EGYPT" (Genesis 45:25). ({SP_(23, 2, "מגיד", "שארץ", "כנען", "גבוהה", "מכל", "הארצות")} "it tells that the land of Canaan is higher than all lands") — \'down\' read literally against four \'up\'s: the compile\'s geography.')
srow(23, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THEY BROUGHT US WORD AND SAID: GOOD IS THE LAND" — DID THEY SPEAK ITS GOOD? THEY SPOKE ITS EVIL! WHO SPOKE ITS GOOD? JOSHUA AND CALEB — AND EVEN SO "YOU WOULD NOT GO UP AND REBELLED" (1:26). ({SP_(23, 3, "מי", "אמר", "טובתה", "יהושע", "וכלב")} "who spoke its good? Joshua and Caleb") — THE INK AGREES: \'good is the land\' two seats, Numbers 14:7 (Joshua and Caleb) and this; the retelling\'s \'they\' is the two, the Sifrei\'s attribution read from the seats.')
srow(24, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU MURMURED IN YOUR TENTS AND SAID: IN HATRED" — THEY SAT IN THEIR DWELLINGS SPEAKING LIKE MOURNERS ("THE WORDS OF A MURMURER ARE AS WOUNDS", Proverbs 26:22) — BUT A KNIFE CAME DOWN FROM HEAVEN AND SPLIT THEIR BELLY ("THEY GO DOWN TO THE CHAMBERS OF THE BELLY"). ({SP_(24, 1, "אבל", "סכין", "ירדה", "מן", "השמים", "ובקעה", "את")} "but a knife came down from heaven and split") — the murmur-verb (three Bible seats, the ink) read by Proverbs\' murmurer.')
srow(24, 2, 'CONTEXT', 'ANOTHER WORD: THEY SAT IN THEIR DWELLINGS WEEPING AS FOR THEIR DEAD, TAKING THEIR SONS: WOE TO YOU, TOMORROW THEY KILL SOME OF YOU, CAPTURE, CRUCIFY; THEIR DAUGHTERS: TOMORROW THEY KILL, CAPTURE, SHAME. The mourning of the tents.')
srow(24, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN THE LORD\'S HATRED OF US" — CAN THE OMNIPRESENT HATE ISRAEL? "I HAVE LOVED YOU, SAYS THE LORD" (Malachi 1:2)! IT IS THEY WHO HATE THE OMNIPRESENT. THE ADAGE: WHAT IS IN YOUR HEART FOR YOUR FRIEND IS IN HIS HEART FOR YOU. ({SP_(24, 3, "אלא", "הם", "ששונאים", "את", "המקום")} "rather it is they who hate the Omnipresent") — the hatred reversed; the ink: \'in hatred\' one seat.')
srow(24, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO GIVE US INTO THE HAND OF THE AMORITE TO DESTROY US" — AS "THE CANAANITE AND ALL THE INHABITANTS WILL HEAR AND SURROUND US AND CUT OFF OUR NAME; WHAT WILL YOU DO FOR YOUR GREAT NAME?" (Joshua 7:9). ({SP_(24, 4, "כענין", "שנאמר", "וישמעו", "הכנעני")} "as it is said: and the Canaanite will hear") — JOSHUA 7:9 brought to 1:27 by the Sifrei: the ink found 7:7\'s \'into the hand of the Amorite\' the shared phrase — the Sifrei cites the next verses of the same prayer (the reference taught).')
srow(25, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHERE ARE WE GOING UP? OUR BROTHERS HAVE MELTED OUR HEART" — THEY SAID: MOSES, HAD WE HEARD THIS FROM OTHERS WE WOULD NOT BELIEVE; BUT FROM MEN WHOSE SONS ARE OUR SONS AND DAUGHTERS OUR DAUGHTERS! ({SP_(25, 1, "אלו", "מבני", "אדם", "אחרים", "היינו", "שומעים")} "had we been hearing from other men") — \'our brothers\' read as the report\'s credit.')
srow(25, 2, 'CONTEXT', '"A PEOPLE GREAT" — TALL OF STATURE. The word read.')
srow(25, 3, 'CONTEXT', '"AND MANY" — MANY IN POPULATION. The word read.')
srow(25, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"CITIES GREAT AND FORTIFIED TO HEAVEN" — RABBAN SHIMON BEN GAMLIEL: THE SCRIPTURES SPEAK IN HYPERBOLE ("HEAR, ISRAEL, YOU CROSS THE JORDAN TODAY", 9:1); BUT WHAT THE OMNIPRESENT SAID TO ABRAHAM — "AS THE STARS OF HEAVEN" (Genesis 26:4), "AS THE DUST OF THE EARTH" (13:16) — IS NO HYPERBOLE. THE HYPERBOLE ROW ({SP_(25, 4, "דברו", "כתובים", "לשון", "הביי")} "the Scriptures spoke the language of hyperbole") — read before by topic in gen_29 (material there) — named, not fresh; the middah: a rule about reading (the hyperbole allowed the text, refused the promise) — the compile\'s docket: which numbers the code takes literally (9:1\'s \'today\' among them).')
srow(25, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND ALSO SONS OF ANAKIM WE SAW THERE" — THEY SAW GIANTS ON GIANTS, AS "THEREFORE PRIDE IS THEIR NECKLACE" (Psalm 73:6). ({SP_(25, 5, "מלמד", "שראו", "שם", "ענקים", "על", "גבי", "ענקים")} "it teaches that they saw there giants upon giants") — the name read by its sound (the necklace-word); the translation\'s \'giants\'.')
srow(25, 6, 'CONTEXT', '"AND I SAID TO YOU" (1:29) — NOT FROM MYSELF BUT FROM THE MOUTH OF THE HOLY ONE. The refrain\'s fourth seat.')
srow(25, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"DREAD NOT NOR FEAR THEM" — WHY? "FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD WHO GOES BEFORE YOU" (1:30): HE WHO DID WONDERS FOR YOU IN EGYPT AND ALL THESE WONDERS WILL DO WONDERS FOR YOU AT YOUR ENTRY. ({SP_(25, 7, "מי", "שעשה", "לכם", "נסים", "במצרים")} "he who did wonders for you in Egypt") — 1:30\'s \'as he did in Egypt\' the ground of 1:29; the ink: \'he will fight for you\' Exodus 14:14\'s.')
srow(25, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"AS ALL HE DID WITH YOU IN EGYPT BEFORE YOUR EYES" — IF YOU DO NOT BELIEVE FOR THE FUTURE, BELIEVE FOR THE PAST. THE SHELF\'S LAST ROW ON CHAPTER 1 ({SP_(25, 8, "אם", "אין", "אתם", "מאמינים", "להבא", "האמינו", "לשעבר")} "if you do not believe for the future, believe for the past"): the Sifrei falls silent from 1:31 to 3:22 — the oath, the defeat, the bypass, Sihon and Og unread by the spine; the outside rows (52:1 Og\'s bed, 199:5 Sihon\'s messengers, 314:2 the carrying father, 37:9 Hermon, 37:11 Pisgah) the only rows on the gap.')
assert sorted(S) == [(p, r) for p in range(18, 26) for r in range(1, SIF_ROWS[p] + 1)], sorted(S)
